# Safety and Git

- Never inspect or print `.env` contents. Never commit `.env` or secrets.
- Commit only when the user explicitly asks. Push, force-push, `reset --hard`, `clean`, and other destructive git/filesystem operations require explicit approval for that action.
- Use local Git for local repo work. Do not add or use GitHub/remote MCP.
- Preserve unrelated user changes. Do not revert work you did not make.
